  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#resolve-a-module-specifier has confused multiple people who don't understand that, via step 1, absolute URLs are allowed. We should add examples of a bunch of valid module specifiers, e.g.:\r\n\r\n- An absolute URL\r\n  - http/https, of course\r\n  - maybe some others, depending on how https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2021 goes\r\n- A scheme-relative URL `//example.com/foo.js`\r\n- Something starting with `./`\r\n- Something starting with `../`\r\n- Something starting with `/` that is a relative URL (not scheme-relative)\r\n- These examples should mix it up between using no file extension, using `.js`, using `.mjs`, using `.js.cgi`, ... anything else we can think of to illustrate that file extension does not matter.",
